{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y2X4P35AjJUzRg6GTFde9W","type":"tool_result","content":"Saved B01.1 = no. Next: B01.2 — Tools discovered from MCP servers are filtered against that allowlist before the model can see or call them.\n  How to verify: 1) Find MCP discovery (`list_tools`, `session.list_tools`, `tools/list`, MCP client setup). 2) Trace the result to where it is handed to the model. 3) Confirm a filter keeps only names on the allowlist. 4) Answer no if any discovered tool reaches the model unfiltered, the filter is a denylist or prefix match (`startswith`, `mcp__server__`), or a refresh or reconnect path skips it.\nSaved B01.2 = no. Next: B01.3 — The dispatcher rejects a call to any tool name not on the allowlist, instead of looking it up dynamically.\n  How to verify: 1) Find the dispatcher (search `tool_use`, `call_tool`, `dispatch`, `execute`, `getattr`, `registry[`). 2) Check it rejects names not on the allowlist with an error. 3) Answer no if it looks tools up with `getattr`, `globals()`, `eval`, or a registry holding more than the allowlist, falls back to calling the MCP server directly, or catches the unknown-tool error and continues.\nSaved B01.3 = no. Next: B01.4 — Allow and approval decisions never read server-supplied hints or descriptions such as `readOnlyHint` or 'read-only'.\n  How to verify: 1) Search for `readOnlyHint`, `destructiveHint`, `annotations`, `description`, and approval or auto-approve code. 2) Check whether any allow, skip-approval, or permission branch reads these. 3) Answer no if any allow or approval decision depends on a server hint or tool description text, including a default that auto-approves tools marked read-only.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65f8d82b-17db-4aa3-8a31-97c7d53b8832","uuid":"1732570a-1a16-49f5-99a7-e23dae845a5d","timestamp":"2026-10-02T17:58:08.034Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Saved B01.1 = no. Next: B01.2 — Tools discovered from MCP servers are filtered against that allowlist before the model can see or call them.\n  How to verify: 1) Find MCP discovery (`list_tools`, `session.list_tools`, `tools/list`, MCP client setup). 2) Trace the result to where it is handed to the model. 3) Confirm a filter keeps only names on the allowlist. 4) Answer no if any discovered tool reaches the model unfiltered, the filter is a denylist or prefix match (`startswith`, `mcp__server__`), or a refresh or reconnect path skips it.\nSaved B01.2 = no. Next: B01.3 — The dispatcher rejects a call to any tool name not on the allowlist, instead of looking it up dynamically.\n  How to verify: 1) Find the dispatcher (search `tool_use`, `call_tool`, `dispatch`, `execute`, `getattr`, `registry[`). 2) Check it rejects names not on the allowlist with an error. 3) Answer no if it looks tools up with `getattr`, `globals()`, `eval`, or a registry holding more than the allowlist, falls back to calling the MCP server directly, or catches the unknown-tool error and continues.\nSaved B01.3 = no. Next: B01.4 — Allow and approval decisions never read server-supplied hints or descriptions such as `readOnlyHint` or 'read-only'.\n  How to verify: 1) Search for `readOnlyHint`, `destructiveHint`, `annotations`, `description`, and approval or auto-approve code. 2) Check whether any allow, skip-approval, or permission branch reads these. 3) Answer no if any allow or approval decision depends on a server hint or tool description text, including a default that auto-approves tools marked read-only.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
