{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdqzHRuS8wse9YRNxziw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed B01–B05 and saved the result to `agent/brace-findings.json`. It passes `validate_findings.py --batch B01,B02,B03,B04,B05 --before-challenges --fix` with no fixes needed: four gaps and one needs_evidence. I did not run challenges, and I did not run the repo's code.\n\n| Item | Rating | Main reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| B01 | gap | The extractor sub-agent runs as `line_item_extractor`, but `tools.yaml` only defines `extractor`. The registry silently falls back to the full procurement tool list (`app/tools/__init__.py:69`). ERP tools found on discovery or refresh are stored with no allowlist filter (`app/mcp_client.py:110`, `:117`). |\n| B02 | gap | `memory_read` takes `business_unit` from an argument the model fills, over a shared database login (`app/tools/memory.py:44`). |\n| B03 | needs_evidence | ERP, payments and Slack tokens come from the token exchange. The database and Anthropic credential sources, token lifetimes, rotation and holder binding are not in the repo. |\n| B04 | gap | The only stop control is checked inside the agent, once at run start (`app/loop.py:127`). Cached tokens are reused with no revocation check and no stated cutoff time (`app/identity.py:97`). |\n| B05 | gap | Payment-affecting ERP operations pass without approval (`app/gate.py:35`). Vendor Slack messages skip approval when the model omits or clears `external` (`app/gate.py:40`). Approvals are not tied to arguments (`app/approvals.py:78`). |\n\n- **B05 ERP path:** the unanchored prefix lets `vendor.update_remit_to`, `invoice.mark_paid` and `invoice.void` through `erp_call`, with write scopes from `config/policy.yaml`.\n- **B05 approvals:** a lookup by tool and target ignores payee, amount and PO lines.\n- **Yes answers:** B01.4, B01.5, B02.4, B03.3 and B05.4 are rated yes, each with a coverage ledger and a counter-search.\n- **Prescan hits:** I confirmed H001 under B05 and dismissed H007. H002–H006 belong to B07–B11 and R05, so I left them for those batches and said so in `scope`.\n- **Not in the repo:** the agent's IAM and RBAC, the token exchange and identity provider setup, how the receiving services validate tokens, and any revocation runbook.\n\nThe helper files I created are `agent/brace-coverage-*.json`, plus `agent/brace-prescan.json` and `agent/brace-inventory.json` from the scripts."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1076,"cache_read_input_tokens":97951,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1076},"output_tokens":804,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65f8d82b-17db-4aa3-8a31-97c7d53b8832","uuid":"594a5b36-d5f1-4e2e-980a-f472d380c7e7","timestamp":"2026-10-02T17:59:19.343Z","request_id":"req_011CfdqzGhFgi5zV5uCAwi3b"}
